determinants multilinearly. Terms with two copies of v vanish by
alternation; terms with one copy become determinants of N rows after
multiplying that row by r. The zero-copy term is also in the ideal.
Consequently adjoining each ordered v_j with r_j v_j already in the
current module costs the product of r_j, not r_j^s. This is exactly
fittingIdeal.triangle, with the earlier v_i in the enlarged module.
For constant-coordinate domain F=O^n and Phi:F→R^s O-linear, set
L=Phi^{-1}(N). The hypothesis pF⊆L, p≠0, gives full-rank Smith form
L=⊕π^{a_i}O in suitable coordinates, a_i≤v(p). Maps F→O/p annihilating
L separate F/L: for a nonzero coordinate modulo π^{a_i}, multiplication
by p/π^{a_i} detects it modulo p. This is also valid for unit p
(the quotient is zero). Thus if all compatible maps kill w then
Phi(w)∈N. This is the exact mem_of_forall_form_eq_zero; no assumption
